  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 230 AM MDT SUN SEP 27 2026\nForecast models depict a building ridge over the southwestern \nU.S. from Tuesday through Thursday, driving lower-elevation \ntemperatures into the upper 70s/low 80s by Wed and Thu. \nThereafter, a weak shortwave trough will enter the Pacific \nNorthwest on Friday, briefly flattening the ridge and dropping \ntemperatures by a few degrees Friday through Saturday. Moisture \nassociated with this trough is likely to remain north, keeping \nsoutheast Oregon and southwest Idaho in a drier airmass. The \nridge is expected to rebound on Sunday as the trough continues \neast, supporting the return of above normal temperatures.",
